<title>FINLAND: Merger hopes in insurance boost Merita.</title>
<headline>Merger hopes in insurance boost Merita.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in banking group Merita Oy set a new 17-month high on Monday on strengthening hopes that Finnish insurer Pohjola and Swedish Skandia would move closer or merge, brokers said.</p>
<p>Merita owns 16 percent of Pohjola's shares.</p>
<p>At 1400/1200 GMT, Merita traded 14.80 markka, up 0.40 markka or almost three percent after touching 14.90 markka. The share last traded at those levels in June 1995.</p>
<p>Turnover was active at over 10 million markka. @</p>
<p>Brokers said the planned merger of Skandia and Swedish Stadshypotek announced in the morning had boosted expectations that Pohjola and Skandia may merge.</p>
<p>&quot;The Skandia and Stadshypotek merger has rekindled hopes of a merger between Skandia and Pohjola,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>-- Veera Heinonen, Helsinki newsroom +358 - 0 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
